\\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   2 \\geq \\sqrt{x}\n   \\]\n   Squaring both sides:\n   \\[\n   4 \\geq x \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x \\leq 4\n   \\]\n\n3. **Outermost square root:**\n   \\[\n   1 - \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{x}} \\geq 0\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   1 \\geq \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{x}}\n   \\]\n   Squaring both sides:\n   \\[\n   1 \\geq 2 - \\sqrt{x}\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( \\sqrt{x} \\):\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{x} \\geq 1\n   \\]\n   Squaring both sides:\n   \\[\n   x \\geq 1\n   \\]\n\nCombining all the conditions \\( x \\geq 0 \\), \\( x \\leq 4 \\), and \\( x \\geq 1 \\), we get:\n\\[\n1 \\leq x \\leq 4\n\\]\n\nThus, the domain of the function \\( f(x) = \\sqrt{1 - \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{x}}} \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{[1, 4]}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{[1, 4]}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:788"}
